# CONFIG's Extended Tuning page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigArducopter.cs.
#
# The claim: SoftwareConfig lists the page for a copter once every parameter is in
# (SoftwareConfig.cs:169), and Activate binds each box and combo to the first of the names the C#
# tries for it that the vehicle has - a box with none stays disabled, named for the first
# (ConfigArducopter.cs:26-204, Controls/MavlinkNumericUpDown.cs:49-122). A box's or a combo's
# change is not written by the control: its ValueUpdated puts it in the page's changes and marks
# it green (ConfigArducopter.cs:260-351), and Write Params - or ctrl+S - writes changes, asking
# first about a value more than double the vehicle's (:353-411). CH9_OPTION has no ValueUpdated
# and writes the moment it changes (Controls/MavlinkComboBox.cs:169-199). The lock is a plain
# check box; it pairs roll and pitch only for names starting RATE_, STB_ or ACRO_, so on this
# vehicle's ATC_RAT_* names a roll change leaves pitch alone, as the C#'s does. Entering a box
# whose parameter 4.7 renamed shows the change under the buttons (:484-501). Refresh Screen reads
# every box's parameter again and runs Activate (:441-477). Each write is proved by the vehicle's
# echo, and put back.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm (the bundled
# 4.8.0-dev copter: RC8_OPTION and RC9_OPTION 0, the roll and pitch rate P gains the firmware's
# 0.135). Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-extended-tuning.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave ATC_RAT_RLL_P at 0.14, or RC8_OPTION or RC9_OPTION at 9;
# the first expectations below then fail until a fresh SITL.

screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# SoftwareConfig adds the page inside `if (gotAllParams)` (SoftwareConfig.cs:148-169), and here
# parameters are downloaded when asked for.
click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.135
expect params.value.ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.135
expect params.value.RC8_OPTION 0
expect params.value.RC9_OPTION 0

click tab-config
expect config.extended.active false
click config-page-ConfigArducopter
settle 1
expect config.page ConfigArducopter
expect config.title Extended Tuning
expect config.extended.active true
expect config.extended.enabled true

# What Activate bound: the first name of each list the vehicle has.
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P.param ATC_RAT_RLL_P
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P.enabled true
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P 0.135
expect config.extended.number.RATE_PIT_P 0.135
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_IMAX.param ATC_RAT_RLL_IMAX
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_FILT.param ATC_RAT_RLL_FLTE
expect config.extended.number.STB_RLL_P.param ATC_ANG_RLL_P
expect config.extended.number.LOITER_LAT_P.param PSC_NE_VEL_P
expect config.extended.number.THR_ALT_P.param PSC_D_POS_P
expect config.extended.number.THR_RATE_P.param PSC_D_VEL_P
expect config.extended.number.WPNAV_SPEED.param WP_SPD
expect config.extended.number.WPNAV_LOIT_SPEED.param LOIT_SPEED_MS
expect config.extended.number.mavlinkNumericUpDownatc_accel_r_max.param ATC_ACC_R_MAX
# A box whose names the vehicle has none of stays disabled, named for the first.
expect config.extended.number.HLD_LAT_P.param HLD_LAT_P
expect config.extended.number.HLD_LAT_P.enabled false
expect config.extended.number.INS_NOTCH_FREQ.enabled false
expect config.extended.combo.TUNE.param TUNE
expect config.extended.combo.CH7_OPTION.param RC7_OPTION
expect config.extended.combo.CH7_OPTION 7
expect config.extended.combo.CH8_OPTION 0
expect config.extended.combo.CH9_OPTION.param RC9_OPTION
expect config.extended.combo.CH9_OPTION.enabled true
# The tool tips: the controls inside the group boxes only, each its parameter and its
# documentation.
expect config.extended.tip.RATE_RLL_P ~ ATC_RAT_RLL_P:
expect config.extended.tip.TUNE none
# Roll and pitch agree and a quad has no H_SWASH_TYPE: the lock stays as the Designer leaves it.
expect config.extended.lock checked
expect config.extended.changes none
expect config.extended.warning none

# Entering a box whose parameter 4.7 renamed shows the change; this SITL is 4.8.
click extended-mavlinkNumericUpDownatc_accel_r_max
expect config.extended.editing mavlinkNumericUpDownatc_accel_r_max
expect config.extended.warning ~ Change in 4.7:
expect config.extended.warning ~ ATC_ACC_R_MAX: units changed from cm/s/s to m/s/s

# A roll gain typed goes into changes and the box turns green; the other box entered hides the
# warning. The lock is checked, but ATC_RAT_RLL_P does not start RATE_: pitch keeps its value.
click extended-RATE_RLL_P
expect config.extended.editing RATE_RLL_P
expect config.extended.warning none
key ctrl+u
type 0.14
key Return
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P 0.140
expect config.extended.changes ATC_RAT_RLL_P=0.14
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P.marked true
expect config.extended.number.RATE_PIT_P 0.135
expect config.extended.number.RATE_PIT_P.marked false
# Nothing is written until Write Params, whose key is ctrl+S.
expect params.value.ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.135
key ctrl+s
settle 2
expect config.extended.write ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.14 accepted
expect params.value.ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.14
expect config.extended.changes none
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P.marked false
expect params.value.ATC_RAT_PIT_P 0.135

# And back, through the button.
click extended-RATE_RLL_P
key ctrl+u
type 0.135
key Return
expect config.extended.changes ATC_RAT_RLL_P=0.135
click extended-BUT_writePIDS
settle 2
expect config.extended.write ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.135 accepted
expect params.value.ATC_RAT_RLL_P 0.135
expect config.extended.changes none

# The lock is a plain check box.
click extended-CHK_lockrollpitch
expect config.extended.lock unchecked
click extended-CHK_lockrollpitch
expect config.extended.lock checked

# RC8's option goes into changes. Camera Trigger is in the first thirty rows of either
# documentation's list, and the list opens at the top for Do Nothing.
click extended-CH8_OPTION
expect config.extended.list.top 0
click extended-CH8_OPTION-9
expect config.extended.combo.CH8_OPTION 9
expect config.extended.combo.CH8_OPTION.text Camera Trigger
expect config.extended.combo.CH8_OPTION.marked true
expect config.extended.changes RC8_OPTION=9
expect params.value.RC8_OPTION 0
# From 0 any option is more than double: Write Params asks first.
click extended-BUT_writePIDS
settle 1
expect config.extended.large RC8_OPTION has more than doubled the last input. Are you sure?
# No puts the vehicle's value back as text, which no row of the list is: the combo keeps its
# choice and changes its value, the colour clears, and nothing is written.
click extended-large-no
settle 1
expect config.extended.large none
expect config.extended.writing false
expect config.extended.combo.CH8_OPTION 9
expect config.extended.combo.CH8_OPTION.marked false
expect config.extended.changes RC8_OPTION=9
expect params.value.RC8_OPTION 0
# Asked again, Yes writes it.
click extended-BUT_writePIDS
settle 1
expect config.extended.large RC8_OPTION has more than doubled the last input. Are you sure?
click extended-large-yes
settle 2
expect config.extended.write RC8_OPTION 9 accepted
expect params.value.RC8_OPTION 9
expect config.extended.changes none
# And back: 0 is not more than double 9, so nothing is asked.
click extended-CH8_OPTION
reveal extended-CH8_OPTION-list extended-CH8_OPTION-0
click extended-CH8_OPTION-0
settle 1
expect config.extended.changes RC8_OPTION=0
click extended-BUT_writePIDS
settle 2
expect config.extended.large none
expect config.extended.write RC8_OPTION 0 accepted
expect params.value.RC8_OPTION 0

# RC9's option has no ValueUpdated: it writes the moment it changes, and changes stays empty.
click extended-CH9_OPTION
click extended-CH9_OPTION-9
settle 2
expect config.extended.changes none
expect config.extended.write RC9_OPTION 9 accepted
expect params.value.RC9_OPTION 9
# The list opens on Camera Trigger; Do Nothing sits further down the documentation's alphabetical
# order, so the wheel brings it into the box first.
click extended-CH9_OPTION
reveal extended-CH9_OPTION-list extended-CH9_OPTION-0
click extended-CH9_OPTION-0
settle 2
expect config.extended.write RC9_OPTION 0 accepted
expect params.value.RC9_OPTION 0
expect config.extended.message none
expect config.extended.writes.pending 0

# Refresh Screen reads each box's parameter again, one at a time - the eleven this vehicle lacks
# each wait out GetParam's retries - then runs Activate.
click extended-BUT_refreshpart
expect config.extended.refreshing true
settle 45
expect config.extended.refreshing false
expect config.extended.number.RATE_RLL_P 0.135
expect config.extended.number.HLD_LAT_P.enabled false
expect config.extended.message none

# Choosing another page hides this one (BackstageView.cs:453-464).
click config-page-ConfigPlanner
expect config.page ConfigPlanner
expect config.extended.active false
